get.description:
Search and retrieve tickets matching your search query. By default, results are sorted by relevance and do not include the ticket description. The following fields are supported by this endpoint:<br><ol><li>search_type - Specifies the search mode. Use 1 for default search or 2 for advanced search.</li><br/><li>search_query - The JSON search object that defines your query. Refer to the format and sample requests below.</li><br/><li>ticket_count - By default you will retrieve 30 tickets per API call. You can customize the count to retrieve 30, 50 or 100 tickets per call.</li><br/><li>offset - Paginate through the resulting ticket list using this field.</li><br/><li>include_description - By default, description is not included in the response. You can include description in the response using this field.</li><br/><li>include_custom_fields - If you use custom ticket fields, you can add them to the response using this field.</li><br/><li>include_survey_details - By default, survey ratings are not included in the response. You can include it in the response using this field.</li><br/><li>nested_fields - If you do not want custom fields and survey details in a nested structure, set this to 1.</li><br/><li>order_by - Sort results by relevance (default), created_time, or updated_time.</li><br/><li>include_merged - Merged tickets are included by default. Set to 0 to exclude merged tickets from the response.</li><br/></ol><h4>Sample search_query for search_type = 1:</h4>For search_type=1 (Default search), use the following search_query format.<br/><pre>{
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"query": "printer not working",
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"search_in": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
}</pre><ol><li>query - The text you want to search for. The query is searched in the fields specified in search_in.</li><br/><li>search_in - An array of integers (1-7) representing the fields to search. If search_in is not specified, the query is searched across all supported fields. The following values are supported:<br/><br/><ul><li>Use 1 for Subject and ticket number - Searches the ticket subject and ticket number.</li><li>Use 2 for Description - Searches the full ticket description.</li><li>Use 3 for Replies and notes - Searches all replies and notes on the ticket.</li><li>Use 4 for Attachment file names - Searches the names of files attached to the ticket.</li><li>Use 5 for Custom ticket fields - Searches across custom text and paragraph field values on the ticket.</li><li>Use 6 for Contacts and companies - Searches the associated contact and company names.</li><li>Use 7 to include archived tickets - Includes archived tickets in the results.</li></ul></li></ol><br/><h4>Sample search_query for search_type = 2:</h4>For search_type=2 (Advanced search), use the following search_query format.<br/><pre>{
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"search_term": [
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"query": "Health concern",
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"search_in": ["subject"]
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;},
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"query": "130,131",
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"search_in": ["ticket_number"]
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;},
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"query": "urgent",
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"search_in": ["cf_priority_note"]
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;]
}</pre><ol><li>query - The text you want to search for. The query is searched in the fields specified in search_in.</li><br/><li>search_in - Specifies the field in which the corresponding query is searched. The query can be searched in subject, ticket_number, or cf_&lt;field_label&gt; (Text and Paragraph custom fields only).</li></ol>The above example searches the subject for &quot;Health concern&quot;, the ticket_number for 130 or 131, and the cf_priority_note custom field for &quot;urgent&quot;. A ticket is returned only if all three conditions match.<br/><br/><h4>Search tips</h4>By default, the search returns tickets that contain all the words in your query, in any order, including possible word variations. Use the following tips to run more specific searches:<br/><ul><li>Use double quotes to find an exact match. For example, <b>&#92;&#92;&quot;desk365&#92;&#92;&quot;</b> finds tickets containing exactly desk365.</li><li>Add an asterisk (&#42;) before the text to find words that end with it. For example, <b>&#42;365</b> will include results like Desk365.</li><li>Add an asterisk (&#42;) before and after the text to find matches that contain it. For example, <b>&#42;pass&#42;</b> will include results like password and compassion.</li></ul><br/><h4>Response field values:</h4><ul><li>For "Priority": Low=1, Medium=5, High=10, Urgent=20.</li><li>For "Source": Email=1, Microsoft Teams=5, Support Portal=6, Phone or Other=7, Web Form=12, Web Widget=13, API=15, Chat Widget (AI Agent)=16, Microsoft Teams(AI Agent)=17, Support Portal (AI Agent)=18</li><li>For first_replied_duration,first_assigned_duration,resolved_duration and closed_duration , the values are represented in minutes.</li><li>For "updated_by_type" and "closed_by_type": System=1, Agent=2, Contact=3.</li><li>For "sv_type": Customer Satisfaction = 1, Five Star Rating = 2, Net Promoter Score = 3.</li><li>For "sv_cs_neutral_type": 'Neither satisfied nor dissatisfied' should be categorized as Positive = 1, Neutral = 2, Negative = 3.</li><li>For "sv_cs_ratings": Possible values are -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3. The text mapped to these values can be retrieved from survey details endpoint for the survey type 'Customer Satisfaction' using sv_name.</li><li>For "conversation_count":Total number of ticket conversations including notes, replies, and forwarded messages.</li></ul><br/><b>Note:</b><ul><li>Search results are limited to a maximum of 1,000 tickets. Results are paginated based on the ticket_count value (30, 50, or 100).</li><li>Each request to this endpoint consumes 5 rate limit tokens due to the resource-intensive nature of full-text search.</li></ul>
